# Scheduler engine (offline tool) — only the pipeline CODE is tracked.
# Everything below is real client data (names, home addresses, phone
# numbers, install dates) and must never be committed, private repo or
# not (user, 2026-08-02). Regenerate locally from the pipeline scripts;
# publish_pages.py pushes the compiled tool straight to Postgres instead
# of a git-tracked file — see backend/app/apis/install_schedule and
# scheduler/RULES.md §12.
scheduler/.venv/
scheduler/__pycache__/
scheduler/cache/
scheduler/review.html
scheduler/map.html
backend/protected/

# The source spreadsheet and every generated workbook -- these are the
# actual client data (names, addresses, phones, emails, install dates),
# not just code that references it. Found tracked in git history on
# 2026-08-02 despite the rest of this section predating it; untracked
# going forward, history purge is a separate decision (destructive,
# needs a force-push -- see conversation).
scheduler/2025 CHRISTMAS CLIENTS (2026 zoning + assignments).xlsx
scheduler/2025 CHRISTMAS CLIENTS (ORIGINAL).xlsx
scheduler/2026 Christmas Schedule.xlsx
scheduler/2026 Team Review.xlsx
scheduler/CHRISTMAS CLIENTS - Storage - Delivery - Install +Takedown.xlsx
scheduler/CHRISTMAS Historical Reference (2024-2025).xlsx

# Every client name schedule.py/rules.py's business rules reference (pins,
# same-day groups, forced-first stops, drops, the one-off manual pairings)
# -- code reads this at runtime instead of embedding names as literals.
scheduler/client_config.json

# The notebook: staff-recorded promised dates. Local working state that
# schedule.py reads on rebuild -- not a source artifact, and also client
# data (see above).
scheduler/overrides.json

# Installer roster seed: real employee names + personal phone numbers.
# Same rule as client_config.json above -- build_review.py reads this at
# build time and bakes it into the shared state's default roster; it never
# belongs in the codebase itself (user, 2026-08-02).
scheduler/roster_seed.json
